## 🍁 HTML Map  
Below is a simple HTML file using map markers with maple leaf emojis 🍁. You can save this as `map.html` and open it in a browser (it uses [Leaflet](https://leafletjs.com/)):

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Smoke Shops Map – Channelview</title>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="initial-scale=1.0">
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet/dist/leaflet.css"
  />
  <style>
    #map { height: 90vh; }
    .emoji-marker {
      font-size: 24px;
      text-shadow: 0 0 2px white;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h2>Smoke Shops near Relax Inn (Channelview, TX)</h2>
  <div id="map"></div>

  <script src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet/dist/leaflet.js"></script>
  <script>
    const map = L.map('map').setView([29.78, -95.12], 13);

    L.tileLayer('https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png', {
      maxZoom: 19,
      attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap contributors'
    }).addTo(map);

    const shops = [
      {
        name: 'Puff’s Smoke Shop',
        coords: [29.7752, -95.0958]
      },
      {
        name: 'Tobacco Mart',
        coords: [29.7855, -95.1247]
      },
      {
        name: 'Channelview Novelties & Smoke Shop',
        coords: [29.7870, -95.1250]
      },
      {
        name: 'House Smoky (East Side)',
        coords: [29.7850, -95.1270]
      }
    ];

    shops.forEach(s => {
      L.marker(s.coords, {
        icon: L.divIcon({
          className: 'emoji-marker',
          html: '🍁',
          iconSize: [24, 24],
          iconAnchor: [12, 12]
        })
      })
      .addTo(map)
      .bindPopup(`<b>${s.name}</b><br/>Coords: ${s.coords[0]}, ${s.coords[1]}`);
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### ✅ How to use:
1. Copy the code above into a text editor.
2. Save the file as **`map.html`**.
3. Open it in any web browser (e.g., Chrome, Safari).
4. You’ll see a zoomable map centered on Channelview with 🍁 markers for each shop.
5. Click a marker to view the shop’s name and exact coordinates.

